shape, till I met you.

258
00:08:55,291 --> 00:08:56,210
-It'll come.

259
00:08:56,210 --> 00:08:57,348
-A heart attack?

260
00:08:57,348 --> 00:08:58,097
Any second.

261
00:08:58,097 --> 00:09:00,853
-When you have to run the
four-minute mile, you'll do it.

262
00:09:00,853 --> 00:09:02,890
-You'll be a Henson
rat, like me.

263
00:09:02,890 --> 00:09:04,787
-I don't think
running's my long suit.

264
00:09:04,787 --> 00:09:05,826
I'll stick to wheels.

265
00:09:05,826 --> 00:09:07,184
At least you don't ride bikes.

266
00:09:07,184 --> 00:09:08,612
-Doodly doodly doodly.

267
00:09:08,612 --> 00:09:10,998
I can't believe
I'm riding a bike!

268
00:09:10,998 --> 00:09:12,376
-It's been a long time.

269
00:09:12,376 --> 00:09:14,004
-Since I rock and rolled?

270
00:09:14,004 --> 00:09:15,492
-Get ready to watch
the A's, old fella?

271
00:09:15,492 --> 00:09:18,757
-Huh?
-What?

272
00:09:18,757 --> 00:09:19,796
-I love buddy films.

273
00:09:19,796 --> 00:09:21,553
This is just like
The Last Boy Scout.

274
00:09:21,553 --> 00:09:24,519
-Really?

275
00:09:24,519 --> 00:09:26,995
-It sounds like Chicago
Tansit Authority.

276
00:09:26,995 --> 00:09:32,318
-[HORN NOISES]

277
00:09:32,318 --> 00:09:33,915
ANNOUNCER: Good afternoon,
ladies and gentlemen.

278
00:09:33,915 --> 00:09:35,703
-Do not take the green acid.
-Whoo.

279
00:09:35,703 --> 00:09:37,430
ANNOUNCER: --Clearwater
motocross championship race.

280
00:09:37,430 --> 00:09:38,788
Hey look, it's
Francis Ford Coppola.

281
00:09:38,788 --> 00:09:40,955
ANNOUNCER: Beautiful sunny
afternoon here at Clearwater.

282
00:09:40,955 --> 00:09:42,523
We'll have a great
day for racing.

283
00:09:42,523 --> 00:09:45,159
-So I come around the
last turn like I'm flying.

284
00:09:45,159 --> 00:09:46,387
Bam, right across
the finish line--

285
00:09:46,387 --> 00:09:47,695
-Wait a minute.

286
00:09:47,695 --> 00:09:49,313
Where did he get that thing?

287
00:09:49,313 --> 00:09:50,641
-Look, I admire your confidence.

288
00:09:50,641 --> 00:09:53,756
But it for some reason or
another, you should lose.

289
00:09:53,756 --> 00:09:55,125
-Easy money.

290
00:09:55,125 --> 00:09:56,712
Hang on to Henry
for me, will you?

291
00:09:56,712 --> 00:09:58,609
He loves the straightaways,
but he hates the turns.

292
00:09:58,609 --> 00:10:00,347
-Anybody catch what he said?
-Nope.

293
00:10:00,347 --> 00:10:03,572
Not a word.

294
00:10:03,572 --> 00:10:05,440
ANNOUNCER: We've got entrants
from all over the country.

295
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:06,228
-All over the world!

296
00:10:06,228 --> 00:10:07,187
ANNOUNCER: Max
Keller will be here,

297
00:10:07,187 --> 00:10:08,106
winner of last year's race.

298
00:10:08,106 --> 00:10:08,605
-Boo.

299
00:10:08,605 --> 00:10:12,519
ANNOUNCER: Our own Chad Webster,
Bill Howard, and Carrie Brown,

300
00:10:12,519 --> 00:10:13,877
representing the cannery.

301
00:10:13,877 --> 00:10:14,377
-Uh oh.

302
00:10:14,377 --> 00:10:15,934
Here come the no-goodniks.

303
00:10:15,934 --> 00:10:17,572
-Yep.

304
00:10:17,572 --> 00:10:18,151
-Why me?

305
00:10:18,151 --> 00:10:20,927
Why me all the time?

306
00:10:20,927 --> 00:10:21,896
-Hey look, it's Malcolm X.

307
00:10:21,896 --> 00:10:23,334
-Oh, I don't think so.

308
00:10:27,178 --> 00:10:28,786
-Got a problem, pal?

309
00:10:28,786 --> 00:10:29,305
-Yeah, man.

310
00:10:29,305 --> 00:10:30,873
I don't like your face.

311
00:10:30,873 --> 00:10:32,730
-Yeah, well you're a jerk.
-Good one.

312
00:10:32,730 --> 00:10:34,388
-Wanna keep all those teeth?

313
00:10:34,388 --> 00:10:35,466
-Check out, Jack.

314
00:10:35,466 --> 00:10:36,924
-Max.
-Stay out of this.

315
00:10:36,924 --> 00:10:37,853
I can handle it.

316
00:10:37,853 --> 00:10:38,641
-It's Meat Loaf.

317
00:10:38,641 --> 00:10:40,429
-Rearranging that mug of
yours might be a challenge.

318
00:10:43,534 --> 00:10:44,992
-D'oh.
-Damn.

319
00:10:44,992 --> 00:10:47,269
I just injected him
with blowfish poison.

320
00:10:47,269 --> 00:10:48,707
-Old Max Keller.

321
00:10:48,707 --> 00:10:49,675
-Still seeing that gerbil?

322
00:10:49,675 --> 00:10:50,684
-How you doing?

323
00:10:50,684 --> 00:10:51,503
Thought you retired.

324
00:10:51,503 --> 00:10:53,061
-I couldn't do that, brother.

325
00:10:53,061 --> 00:10:55,267
Besides, busting up
towns ain't cool anymore.

326
00:10:55,267 --> 00:10:56,835
-They must have gone to
speech, class together.

327
00:10:56,835 --> 00:10:58,033
-I would find you here.

328
00:10:58,033 --> 00:11:00,410
You any better with
that bike of yours now?

329
00:11:00,410 --> 00:11:02,257
-I always beat you, didn't I?

330
00:11:02,257 --> 00:11:04,744
Hey, Hog, this the
Ma-- uh, McAllister.

331
00:11:04,744 --> 00:11:06,870
-Uh, this is my elderly
gentleman friend.

332
00:11:06,870 --> 00:11:08,888
-Best biker around.

333
00:11:08,888 --> 00:11:09,387
-My.

334
00:11:09,387 --> 00:11:10,785
So why do they call you Hog?

335
00:11:10,785 --> 00:11:13,511
-You better just watch.
MCALLISTER: That's good advice.

336
00:11:13,511 --> 00:11:15,828
-Ebony at ivory.

337
00:11:15,828 --> 00:11:18,164
-Hm.

338
00:11:18,164 --> 00:11:20,281
-Hey, I got walnuts in there.

339
00:11:20,281 --> 00:11:22,168
[ENGINE NOISE]

340
00:11:22,168 --> 00:11:24,984
-He's starting up
the guy's hand.

341
00:11:24,984 --> 00:11:26,153
-That thing hasn't
worked in years.

342
00:11:26,153 --> 00:11:27,441
Thank you.

343
00:11:27,441 --> 00:11:29,268
-Good night.

344
00:11:29,268 --> 00:11:30,187
-Yeah, thanks.

345
00:11:30,187 --> 00:11:31,864
See you later, Hog.

346
00:11:31,864 --> 00:11:33,971
-Uh, nice meeting
you, Mr. Pig, was it?

347
00:11:33,971 --> 00:11:35,379
Oh, Hog.

348
00:11:35,379 --> 00:11:37,726
That's it.

349
00:11:37,726 --> 00:11:40,372
-Brrrrrrrm

350
00:11:40,372 --> 00:11:42,589
-Well, nice company you keep.

351
00:11:42,589 --> 00:11:44,316
-Ah, he's a pussycat.

352
00:11:44,316 --> 00:11:45,914
What'd you do to him anyway?

353
00:11:45,914 --> 00:11:47,412
-Oh, just being friendly.

354
00:11:47,412 --> 00:11:49,499
-Hope he can still
hold the handlebar.

355
00:11:49,499 --> 00:11:51,805
-Well, see you for the
champagne at the finish line.

356
00:11:51,805 --> 00:11:55,051
-Um, pick up some
cedar chips for Muffy.

357
00:11:55,051 --> 00:11:56,868
-Hey, easy on the gerbil, Lee.

358
00:11:56,868 --> 00:11:57,807
Hey, whoa.

359
00:11:57,807 --> 00:11:59,854
-Things are not
what they seem, Lee.

360
00:11:59,854 --> 00:12:00,922
ANNOUNCER: Big crowd today.

361
00:12:00,922 --> 00:12:02,460
We appreciate that, folks.

362
00:12:02,460 --> 00:12:03,748
Always great to see you.

363
00:12:03,748 --> 00:12:06,055
-Uh, believe me, it's
really a big crowd.

364
00:12:06,055 --> 00:12:07,942
ANNOUNCER: Going to be a
lot of fun out here today.

365
00:12:07,942 --> 00:12:10,738
You're going to see
some great bike racing.

366
00:12:10,738 --> 00:12:11,507
-Hi.

367
00:12:11,507 --> 00:12:13,783
-Looks like the camera
lost interest in Timothy.

368
00:12:13,783 --> 00:12:15,341
-I can see that.
-What do you want?

369
00:12:15,341 --> 00:12:17,438
-Isn't that the kid
who won last year?

370
00:12:17,438 --> 00:12:19,335
-I don't remember.

371
00:12:19,335 --> 00:12:21,123
-I know him

372
00:12:21,123 --> 00:12:22,181
-Well, tell him.

373
00:12:22,181 --> 00:12:23,919
I'm not interested.

374
00:12:23,919 --> 00:12:25,157
-You are so tough.
-Familiar.

375
00:12:25,157 --> 00:12:26,785
-You know, one of these
days, that mouth of yours

376
00:12:26,785 --> 00:12:28,203
is going to get you
in a lot of trouble.

377
00:12:28,203 --> 00:12:28,702
I--

378
00:12:28,702 --> 00:12:30,759
-And you what?

379
00:12:30,759 --> 00:12:32,586
Take a walk, Webster.
-Listen,--

380
00:12:32,586 --> 00:12:34,404
-It's on the tip of my tongue.

381
00:12:34,404 --> 00:12:37,669
-This race track is one place
in this town you don't own.

382
00:12:37,669 --> 00:12:39,137
-It's Scott Hamilton!

383
00:12:39,137 --> 00:12:40,045
That's who it is!

384
00:12:40,045 --> 00:12:43,071
-Out here, you've got to
beat me fair and square.

385
00:12:43,071 --> 00:12:44,639
-Ooh, she's a little spitfire.

386
00:12:44,639 --> 00:12:46,177
-Grr.

387
00:12:46,177 --> 00:12:47,445
-Unless, of course,
you're too gutless

388
00:12:47,445 --> 00:12:50,251
to try without your daddy's
money to back you up.

389
00:12:50,251 --> 00:12:51,209
-D'oh!

390
00:12:51,209 --> 00:12:52,148
-Pearl drops.

391
00:12:52,148 --> 00:13:00,036
Mmm.

392
00:13:00,036 --> 00:13:01,235
-It's a Ren Fest.

393
00:13:01,235 --> 00:13:01,754
-Mmm.

394
00:13:01,754 --> 00:13:03,002
ANNOUNCER: Just a
few more seconds

395
00:13:03,002 --> 00:13:04,600
before the gun goes off.

396
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:06,407
All jockeying for position.

397
00:13:06,407 --> 00:13:09,173
-[ENGINE NOISES WITH MOUTH]

398
00:13:09,173 --> 00:13:11,460
-They all look so good.

399
00:13:11,460 --> 00:13:13,367
[ENGINE NOISE]

400
00:13:13,367 --> 00:13:17,172
-[ENGINE NOISES WITH MOUTH]
ANNOUNCER: There's the gun.

401
00:13:17,172 --> 00:13:19,089
And they're off.

402
00:13:19,089 --> 00:13:21,146
-Go Charlie Brown, Go!

403
00:13:21,146 --> 00:13:23,233
ANNOUNCER: But Max Keller
is right behind him.

404
00:13:23,233 --> 00:13:25,240
And I can see Big Jim Stevenson.

405
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:26,488
-Big Jim Seaborn?

406
00:13:26,488 --> 00:13:27,477
ANNOUNCER: With friends.

407
00:13:27,477 --> 00:13:28,455
And enemies.

408
00:13:28,455 --> 00:13:29,933
Number 11.

409
00:13:29,933 --> 00:13:31,900
And there's Carrie Brown,
coming up fast on the inside.

410
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:34,926
-And there's Linda Ronstadt
behind him on roller skates!

411
00:13:34,926 --> 00:13:37,422
ANNOUNCER: Uh oh.
Uh oh, there's a pile-up.

412
00:13:37,422 --> 00:13:38,860
Doesn't look as
if anybody's hurt.

413
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:40,977
-Well, we can dream, can't we?

414
00:13:40,977 --> 00:13:42,245
ANNOUNCER: Racing
can be pretty rough.

415
00:13:42,245 --> 00:13:43,064
-Nice PA.

416
00:13:43,064 --> 00:13:44,562
-William Katt, Freddy Mercury.

417
00:13:49,595 --> 00:13:51,512
-Oh.

418
00:13:51,512 --> 00:13:53,379
ANNOUNCER: Nine to ten
racers have pulled away now.

419
00:13:53,379 --> 00:13:55,826
They leave the pack
behind in a cloud of dust.

420
00:13:55,826 --> 00:13:57,283
It's going to be a close finish.

421
00:13:57,283 --> 00:13:59,241
-Here's my favorite.

422
00:13:59,241 --> 00:14:01,677
ANNOUNCER: Carrie
Brown, still the leader.

423
00:14:01,677 --> 00:14:05,102
-Nothing like enjoying nature
on a screaming crotch rocket.

424
00:14:05,102 --> 00:14:08,517
-Mhm.
-Oof.

425
00:14:08,517 --> 00:14:10,215
-Looks like Tony Scott directed.

426
00:14:13,120 --> 00:14:24,164
-This week on "Then
Came Bronson."

427
00:14:24,164 --> 00:14:25,572
ANNOUNCER: Here they are!

428
00:14:25,572 --> 00:14:27,380
-Hey, he's breaking
into somebody's van.

429
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:31,214
ANNOUNCER: Max Keller and
Carrie Brown all the way.

430
00:14:31,214 --> 00:14:32,652
They cross the finish line.

431
00:14:32,652 --> 00:14:34,070
-Here they come.

432
00:14:34,070 --> 00:14:35,069
-Oof.
-Oof.

433
00:14:35,069 --> 00:14:35,728
-Oh!

434
00:14:35,728 --> 00:14:36,686
Human speedbump.

435
00:14:36,686 --> 00:14:39,302
-Ooh.
-Hey.

436
00:14:39,302 --> 00:14:40,860
You all right?
What's the matter with that guy?

437
00:14:40,860 --> 00:14:41,589
-I'm alive.

438
00:14:41,589 --> 00:14:42,488
-She lives!

439
00:14:42,488 --> 00:14:43,746
She lives!
Hoo-hoo!

440
00:14:43,746 --> 00:14:47,371
-Yay.

441
00:14:51,495 --> 00:14:52,873
-Max, I lost the hamster.

442
00:14:52,873 --> 00:14:54,181
-Is she OK?

443
00:14:54,181 --> 00:14:54,720
-OK?

444
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:55,719
Yeah, she's OK.

445
00:14:55,719 --> 00:14:57,187
She won the race.

446
00:14:57,187 --> 00:14:58,365
-Even Ali lost a few.

447
00:14:58,365 --> 00:15:01,251
-Yeah, but never to a
girl with a shag haircut.

448
00:15:01,251 --> 00:15:04,047
Well, OK, once.

449
00:15:04,047 --> 00:15:05,455
-Thanks!

450
00:15:05,455 --> 00:15:06,433
-Nice race.

451
00:15:06,433 --> 00:15:08,770
Never lost it before.
-Can I carry your bike home?

452
00:15:08,770 --> 00:15:09,888
-Well, I have.

453
00:15:09,888 --> 00:15:11,056
-Shame about your bike.

454
00:15:11,056 --> 00:15:12,544
Guys play rough around here.

455
00:15:12,544 --> 00:15:14,491
-Yeah, I know.
-Ooh.

456
00:15:14,491 --> 00:15:15,979
-You're pretty good.

457
00:15:15,979 --> 00:15:16,958
You almost beat me.

458
00:15:16,958 --> 00:15:17,457
-D'oh!

459
00:15:17,457 --> 00:15:18,875
-That was the idea.

460
00:15:18,875 --> 00:15:20,503
-So, uh, how about a
little victory party?

461
00:15:20,503 --> 00:15:21,951
-I got a gerbil.

462
00:15:21,951 --> 00:15:23,878
-At least dinner.

463
00:15:23,878 --> 00:15:27,343
-Well, um, I have to work
the early shift tomorrow.

464
00:15:27,343 --> 00:15:28,831
And I don't even know you.

465
00:15:28,831 --> 00:15:29,919
-So OK.

466
00:15:29,919 --> 00:15:31,677
-You don't have
to buy me dinner.

467
00:15:31,677 --> 00:15:33,334
-I was thinking you might buy.

468
00:15:33,334 --> 00:15:34,822
-Oh.
-Ooh.

469
00:15:34,822 --> 00:15:36,500
-I mean, you won
all my prize money.

470
00:15:36,500 --> 00:15:38,906
-I'll think it over.

471
00:15:38,906 --> 00:15:41,213
-Uh, gee, that could
have gone better.

472
00:15:41,213 --> 00:15:43,769
Well, I didn't want her anyway,

473
00:15:43,769 --> 00:15:45,417
-I'm not used to seeing
them walk away from you.

474
00:15:45,417 --> 00:15:46,655
-Usually they run, screaming.

475
00:15:46,655 --> 00:15:49,311
-Lose one, you lose another.
-D'oh.

476
00:15:49,311 --> 00:15:51,588
-Good looking girl,
though, isn't she?

477
00:15:51,588 --> 00:15:54,613
Or does your ninja discipline
make you immune to such things?

478
00:15:54,613 --> 00:15:57,140
-There are certain yearnings
one does not want to overcome.

479
00:15:57,140 --> 00:15:59,956
-Besides, I took a shuriken
wheel in the whipper, once.

480
00:15:59,956 --> 00:16:01,443
-Ow.

481
00:16:01,443 --> 00:16:04,749
-Come on, Boss.

482
00:16:04,749 --> 00:16:06,236
-Oh, is there going
to be a boat race?

483
00:16:09,592 --> 00:16:11,089
-It's a secret meeting
of all those people

484
00:16:11,089 --> 00:16:12,777
who want this show canceled.

485
00:16:12,777 --> 00:16:15,503
-Oh, grab a leaflet, please.

486
00:16:15,503 --> 00:16:17,151
-"F.I.S.T." with
Sylvester Stallone.

487
00:16:17,151 --> 00:16:18,998
-Grab a leaflet, please.

488
00:16:18,998 --> 00:16:19,927
Union meeting tomorrow.

489
00:16:19,927 --> 00:16:21,315
Don't forget.

490
00:16:21,315 --> 00:16:22,972
-Oh, uh, it's a
Clifford Odets play.

491
00:16:22,972 --> 00:16:24,380
-No, a Tom Bodett play.

492
00:16:24,380 --> 00:16:24,929
-Oh.

493
00:16:24,929 --> 00:16:26,148
-Huh?
-Huh?

494
00:16:26,148 --> 00:16:27,006
-Hey.

495
00:16:27,006 --> 00:16:28,135
-Still at it, huh, Carrie?

496
00:16:28,135 --> 00:16:30,242
-I don't quit, Harold.

497
00:16:30,242 --> 00:16:31,470
-Ossie Davis?

498
00:16:31,470 --> 00:16:32,608
-Here, have a leaflet.

499
00:16:32,608 --> 00:16:33,986
-Hey, Pippi Longstocking.

500
00:16:33,986 --> 00:16:34,795
-Another meeting?

501
00:16:34,795 --> 00:16:35,973
You bet.

502
00:16:35,973 --> 00:16:37,421
-Tomorrow afternoon.

503
00:16:37,421 --> 00:16:40,786
And the-- we're
counting on you, Amy.

504
00:16:40,786 --> 00:16:42,214
We just need a few
more signatures.

505
00:16:42,214 --> 00:16:42,714
-Sure, sure.

506
00:16:42,714 --> 00:16:45,230
-When are you going to let
me take you dancing, Carrie?

507
00:16:45,230 --> 00:16:46,778
-When "Welcome Back
Kotter" is canceled.

508
00:16:46,778 --> 00:16:47,277
-Heh.

509
00:16:47,277 --> 00:16:49,913
-You sign this petition,
we'll talk about it.

510
00:16:49,913 --> 00:16:50,882
-All right.

511
00:16:55,725 --> 00:16:56,613
-Come on, Max.

512
00:16:56,613 --> 00:17:01,416
I know she rejected you,
but we've got to try again.

513
00:17:01,416 --> 00:17:03,443
-Well, this is it.

514
00:17:03,443 --> 00:17:04,921
Clearwater cannery.

515
00:17:04,921 --> 00:17:05,620
-Sure is dirty.

516
00:17:05,620 --> 00:17:09,714
-Nerve center of the
city, such as it is.

517
